  "contract": {
    "binding": "Explicit X86InstructionDebugProfile::ExecuteBreakpoints; X86LegacyDebugProfile aliases the shared type. Debug banks add DR0-DR3; no V6 wire-layout or stable SDK C-ABI change. Existing InstructionStep remains the default.",
    "controls": "Local/global enables and ignored LE/GE accepted, bit 10 set, all RW/LEN fields zero, remaining DR7/DEBUGCTL bits zero. Reserved/high DR6 bits checked. Data/I/O watchpoints, GD, RTM/PT and BTF are explicit refusals.",
    "addresses": "First original instruction byte only, including the first prefix. i386 wraps CS.base+EIP to 32 bits; x64 uses the full linear address. Compatibility return targets use wrapped CS.base+IP for matching while saving the IP offset in the debug frame. Noncanonical DR addresses are legal values and do not match an admitted canonical PC.",
    "priority": "Eligible IRQ/NMI and PVI pending-interrupt #GP precede execute breakpoints. Execute breakpoints precede original fetch, page/segment faults, byte authentication and instruction effects.",
    "inhibition": "RF and the incoming MOV/POP-SS window suppress the execute fault without deferring a cause. Completed instructions clear RF; unfinished REP and IRET restoration use their existing owners.",
    "status": "Report only enabled matching B0-B3 slots, retaining sticky status and setting RTM. TF can combine BS with matching next-PC comparators when RF permits. ICEBP remains separate. Disabled-slot behavior is a qualified processor choice.",
    "restart": "An execute fault saves the original PC and entry RF=0. Original handlers set saved RF and IRET to execute the target once. DR6 survives failed IDT entry and accepted-event backing continuation without refetch or re-publication.",
    "legacy_oracle": "Original bytes with KVM guest debugging disabled; compare DR6/DR7, eight GPRs, six caches, EIP/EFLAGS/CR2, shadows/NMI state and all 2 MiB RAM. Legacy/PAE paging, independent 16/32-bit code/stack/gate widths, CPL0/3, 16 instruction/environment scenarios and 13 comparator configurations.",
    "x64_oracle": "Original bytes with KVM guest debugging disabled; compare DR6/DR7, represented 16-GPR/segment state, RIP/RFLAGS/CR2, NMI/shadows and all 256 KiB RAM. Preseed page A/D bits to isolate the final HLT fetch. CPL0-3, 21 instruction/environment scenarios, 13 comparator configurations, four TF/RF combinations, original IRET and REP paths, failed gate/stack entry and eligible/masked IRQ/NMI.",
    "round_trips": "Original handlers set RF, clear TF where needed, count entry and IRET. x64 additionally repairs a subsequent operand #PF before retry, preserving exactly-once original instruction effects. No host repair inside the native program.",
    "compatibility_return_oracle": "All IRET/RETF widths, compatibility CS.D values, CPL0-3, zero/nonzero/wrapping CS bases, restored RF and linear-versus-offset comparators. Input GPR high halves and explicit choices are zero; full post-event state and RAM are compared without masking.",
    "build_matrix": "Fork and production r6 SDK; P and E cores; x64 HighC/LLVM-to-C through Clang/NeverC at O0/O2."
  },
